[#:seon.task{:name "a-stored-namespace-replacement-keeps-removed-components"
             :plan "`seon.turn.batch/namespace-facts` selects the stored namespace by the keys of the context row from `seon.sci.eval/namespace-context-row`; `seon.program/canonical-row` drops an empty component collection (absence), so a namespace whose agent removed its last require, alias, import, refer or fixture keeps the stored ones. Select the stored entity by the resolver-context attributes `seon.sci.eval/binding-rows` owns, so `seon.program/exact-replacement-tx` retracts what the context no longer holds, and re-creates no unchanged alias component."}
 #:seon.task{:name "tests-read-forms-through-a-stage-no-entrant-uses",
            :plan
            "`seon.test-support/evaluate` and code-request read a source through `seon.turn.batch/code-request` (`seon.sci.forgive/read-state` plus `seon.sci.batch/read-next`: one live read over the whole text), while every production SCI entrant (MCP eval_clj via `seon.cluster.agent/submit-source!` and `seon.turn/code-sources`, and model replies via `seon.turn/planned-sources`) segments first (`seon.sci.forgive/segments`, structural reads) and then reads each row again (`seon.turn/read-row`). `seon.turn.batch/turn-request` and seon.sci.batch/read-code have no caller. Tests therefore prove a read stage no entrant runs. Correct: one read stage, used by tests and every entrant; the uncalled ones deleted. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/plan-research/r-read-notes.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-declared-var-call-stores-no-edge"
  :plan "A call to a Var that is declared but has no definition entity stores no call edge. Reproduce (MCP eval_clj sci, one pass): (declare zz) then (defn calls-zz [] (zz)) stores calls [clojure.core/defn] with no edge to scratch.macro/zz, although derive-form adds the declared Vars to the analysis prelude so that a call to one is an edge. Cause unverified (suspect the edge is dropped because no entity exists for zz). Correct: the stored call edge names the declared Var, and resolves to its entity when that is defined. Proof: a test through the agent entrance running (declare zz) and (defn calls-zz [] (zz)) in one pass asserts calls-zz's `:seon.fn/calls` contains the zz symbol. Read `seon.turn.batch/derive-form` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/s5-admission/macro-design.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "analysis-uses-the-namespace-row-after-the-form"
  :plan "derive-form analyzes a defining form with the namespace row left after the form, not the row the definition ran under. Reproduce (MCP eval_clj sci, namespace probe.alias5, x -> clojure.string): (do (defn h [] (x/upper-case \"a\")) (alias 'x 'clojure.set)) answers nil and h is ADMITTED with calls [defn clojure.set/upper-case], an edge to a Var that does not exist; SCI resolved x/upper-case to clojure.string/upper-case when it evaluated the defn. Correct: each form is analyzed under the namespace row in force when it was evaluated. Proof: that form stores calls [defn clojure.string/upper-case] or is refused, never the false edge. Read `seon.fn/runtime-analysis-batch`, `seon.turn.batch/derive-form` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/s5-admission/alias-design.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-unjoined-definition-write-is-silent"
  :plan "When join-write answers :no-definition-at-origin the definition is not admitted, and the pass records nothing and says nothing: no note and no error. Correct: an unanalyzed note (an error value delivered in the reply) names the Var and the origin that joined no analyzed definition. Proof: a definition write whose origin joins no analyzed form answers a diagnostic naming it. Read `seon.turn.batch/join-write` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/s5-admission/prose-design.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-jvm-compile-error-shows-the-wrapper-message"
             :plan "JVM-mode (undefined-jvm-sym) through MCP answers `:seon.error/message` \"Syntax error compiling at (1:1).\" twice (top and first chain link) with the cause, Unable to resolve symbol, last in :chain (default 2026-10-08). clojure.main/err->msg (ex-triage + ex-str) is Clojure's own message for this. Done when the reply's message is the triaged cause and a regression asserts it. Read `seon.turn.batch/jvm-request` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/agent-messages/messages-opus-messages.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-core-unmap-with-a-surviving-caller-is-silently-undone"
             :plan "On an agent's own branch (default, MCP SCI, agent plan-review-opus-probe, 2026-10-08): (defn pa [x] x) (defn pb [x] (pa x)) then (ns-unmap *ns* 'pa), in the same pass or a later one, answers nil with no diagnostic, yet [`:seon.fn/sym` scratch.prv/pa] stays stored and the next pass resolves #'scratch.prv/pa again: the unmap is undone. Cause: removal-facts returns my.program's deletion refusal when referrers survive, the pass keeps the rest of the facts, and acquisition reinstalls the stored row. The P1 commit (ded5e35de) says the write observer already stores the final state; true only with no surviving referrer. Correct (owner REPL law, repl-plan P8): store the final state (pa retracted, pb kept with its calls edge) and deliver one finding naming pb beside the value; integrity is judged at merge (the evidence M5). Proof: a seon.repl-differential test row asserting pa absent from the store and the finding present after the pass. Read `seon.turn.batch/form-facts`, `seon.turn.batch/removal-facts`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/review/plan-review-opus-plan-review.md` and `docs/seon/specs/merge.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-repl-namespace-row-keeps-neither-doc-nor-source"
             :plan "A namespace created at the REPL is stored as `(ns rtefix2.core)` with no docstring, and evaluating its full `ns` form again does not update the row (`seon.turn.batch/namespace-facts` writes a stored namespace only when its resolver state changed, and `seon.sci.eval/namespace-context-row` derives source and doc from the reader context, not the `ns` form). Its digest then never equals the file's, so the branch-evidence gate reports every agent-authored namespace as differing. High priority for the dogfood loop. Done when evaluating an `ns` form stores that form's docstring and source, and the digest equals the one indexing its file produces. Reported by lane repl-test-edges. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/dogfood/pilot.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-display-budget-has-no-feedback"
             :plan "Every evaluation records `:seon.eval/shown-tokens`, `:seon.eval/value-tokens`, `:seon.eval/elisions` and `:seon.eval/value-class`, but not which cuts were made or whether the agent dug in afterwards, so the 1,500-token budget and the 32-child cap are guesses (census of 40 forms, default 2026-10-08). Done when settlement records each reply's cut paths and the later forms that read the result handle (ledger D1, `:seon.cluster.eval/result-reads`), and a report per value class gives elided count, dig-in rate, override use and a recommended budget. Read `seon.turn.batch/settle` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/reply-census/reply-census.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-failed-defn-after-in-ns-leaves-an-unbound-stub-var"
             :plan "Observed (branch impl-cs01c5, 2026-10-08) ran (in-ns 'some.source.ns) and then a defn that was partial or failed, and found an unbound stub Var left in that namespace on its branch (seen on the Var `based-file`). A defn that does not complete must leave the namespace as it was, as Clojure's own failed def would not bind a usable Var. Reproduced with a deftest, and the stub then blocks recording silently (live-agent run 3, default 0de932400, root on main, 2026-10-08): (ns live.scratch3-test (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]])) then (deftest ^{:seon/tasks #{live.text/slug-joins-words}} first-fails-probe (is (= 1 1))) fails 'Unable to resolve symbol' (the tag set unquoted); the corrected (deftest first-fails-probe (is (= 1 1))) in a later eval request answers {:seon.render.var/symbol live.scratch3-test/first-fails-probe} with no error or diagnostic, yet no :seon.test/sym row is ever written, on that or any later evaluation of the same name, and the step never runs it. The same deftest under a fresh name records at once. So a task's proof whose first evaluation failed never becomes a proof (root's seon.task/assign! refused :no-proofs). Done when a failed or partial def leaves no Var behind (or the stub is reported as a finding naming it) and a later successful evaluation of that name records its declaration, with a regression through MCP SCI asserting the namespace's Vars and the recorded test row. Read `seon.sci.eval/build-base-ctx` and `seon.turn.batch/derive-form`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "redefining-a-file-function-in-seon-error-is-refused-by-its-digest"
             :plan "On a fresh agent branch (agent nilable-rule-wb, default JVM before e40167fbe, 2026-10-09), (in-ns 'seon.error) then a docstring-only (defn throwable? ...) with its committed contract is refused by the writer: 'The stored definition digest of [:seon.fn/sym seon.error/throwable?] is not the one its definition produces' (the pass's digest and the writer's differ). The same refusal followed (require 'malli.core 'malli.error) on another agent. seon.render.ns/first-doc-line redefines without it, so the difference is in seon.error's namespace context (its :as-alias flow require, or a core predicate registration). Done when a REPL redefinition of a seon.error function with an unchanged contract is admitted, regression through seon.mcp/call. Read `seon.db/definition-digest-of`, `seon.error/throwable?` and `seon.turn.batch/analyzed-entities`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-refused-remove-ns-still-removes-the-namespace-from-the-context"
             :plan "Agent fan9b-anchor (fan-out 9b, default f54e73c83, 2026-10-09) evaluated `(remove-ns 'seon.ref)` on its branch. The reply refused it (\"Not admitted to the program: its program facts were refused ... Cannot perform seon.turn.batch/removal-facts on seon.ref; repair the named referrers first.\"), yet its next form `(clojure.core/ns-unmap 'seon.ref 'common-prefix)` answered \"No namespace: seon.ref found\": the SCI context had dropped the namespace the program kept, and the agent stopped working (7 calls, task not done). Done when a removal whose program facts are refused leaves the agent's SCI context holding the namespace, so the context and the branch's program agree. Read `my.program/remove-ns!` and `seon.turn.batch/removal-facts`."}

 #:seon.task{:name "only-root-holds-a-host-evaluator"
  :plan "Fence outside the night (no-fences law): `seon.turn.batch/jvm-evaluate` refuses any agent whose id is not the string \"root\" (e361536a9), and `seon.test/root-agent?` decides compiled versus interpreted by the same string, while `seon.sci.eval/host-namespace!` stays reachable from the core loader. Root design: a non-root agent's world is built with no host evaluator and no host-loading path at all (its SCI context has no `eval` of host forms and its loader interprets from rows), so the refusal cannot be reached and the string comparison goes; root's world is the one built with them. Done when `seon.turn.batch/jvm-evaluate` carries no agent-id check and a non-root agent's JVM-mode request has no host evaluator to call."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-jvm-batch-answers-the-forms-around-a-failed-read"
  :plan "`seon.cluster.evaluate-source-test/a-failed-read-is-its-forms-error-and-reading-continues-in-sci-and-jvm` is red at HEAD 6a421d96e (check run eb451aab3a4d, evaluate_source_test.clj:280): for the text `(+ 1 1)` `(vector ::nope.alias/k)` `(+ 2 2)` the SCI half answers [2 nil 4], but `seon.batch/evaluate-batch` over `seon.turn.batch/jvm-request` answers `:seon.batch/value` [nil nil nil]: JVM mode evaluates none of the forms around the unreadable one. One REPL path reads each form once and continues after a read error in both evaluators. Done when the JVM batch answers [2 nil 4] with the reader error (`:seon.sci.reader/form`) on the second entry, fixed in the JVM reader or evaluate stage, not in the test."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-new-agents-first-request-costs-twenty-seconds"
             :plan "The first `eval_clj` request of a new agent id (`printer-p1a`, mode jvm, two forms, both refused by `seon.turn.batch/jvm-evaluate` as not root) answered with `:seon.cost` 21,498 ms, 2,113 calls and 589 MB on 2026-10-16; the same two forms as root took 70 ms. The cost is the new agent's branch and context on first use, not the refusal. Ordinary work is sub-second: name the instrumented functions responsible (`seon.profile/measure` on the first request of a fresh agent id) and make the first request cost what branch creation (`d/branch!`, a pointer) and a context fork must do. Read `seon.turn.batch/jvm-evaluate` and `seon.mcp/call`."}]
